From b941b908232b08d4680937f923441d393a450207 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:05:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Capture's thumbnail can be dragged into apps

The floating thumbnail after a screenshot or recording can be dragged, like a
file, into any app: a chat, a document, a folder. A click still opens it, and
a drop leaves the file where it was saved and puts the thumbnail away.

The Shell cannot start a Wayland drag, so a small helper,
luma-capture-drag (GTK 4, in libexecdir), is started as the Shell's own
Wayland client (Meta.WaylandClient). Its window is hidden from the window
list, kept above other windows and on every workspace, never keeps the
keyboard, and is laid transparently over the thumbnail the Shell draws. It
reports hover, clicks and drags on stdout and takes show and hide commands
on stdin, and exits after two idle minutes.

A drag offers the file (text/uri-list, and the portal file transfer where a
portal runs) and GNOME's x-special/gnome-copied-files, with a small picture
of the capture as the drag icon; Mutter carries the drag to Xwayland apps.
It does not offer image/png: GTK apps that accept both, Files among them,
take the image data and save "Dropped Image.png" instead of the file. The
screenshot is still on the clipboard as image/png.

Also: the thumbnail image no longer asks St for background-position: center,
which St ignored with a warning.
